  "fixes": [
    "Derive Flight input limits from checksum and record passes instead of one physical file size.",
    "Retain compact physical records; reuse final register snapshot values and canonical JSON buffers; reserve known Flight event counts and discontinuity capacity under allocation guards.",
    "Validate cached Flight discontinuity evidence by its canonical union without changing individual event facts, causes, domains or provenance.",
    "Bound discontinuity payload totals by max(16 MiB, rows * 256 B), retain the 1 MiB per-payload cap, byte accounting, cancellation and allocation checks.",
    "Reuse QueryContext validated gap evidence for register replay and memory analysis. Store global register invalidations once, apply them lazily per thread, and query from the latest invalidation or checkpoint.",
    "Charge memory posting/sort work to Nodes, returned byte-address/history rows to Rows. Retain both 2,000 response rows and the 100,000-node interactive cap.",
    "Use a binary-searched gap prefix for memory state so future gaps do not consume past-history capacity. Preserve unordered future cross-thread write conflict checks."
  ],
